            <ArticleTitle>[Mixed neuroglial tumor: description of a case].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>57-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of neuroglial tumor in a 18-year-old man is presented. The neoplasm was composed by two cell types. One type showed features typical of neuronal cells, while the other resembled glial cells. The diagnosis was confirmed by immunohistochemistry results.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
